# XSS (Cross-Site Scripting) Prevention Rules

## Overview
Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities occur when user-supplied data is rendered in HTML without proper sanitization, allowing attackers to inject malicious scripts that execute in other users' browsers.

## Critical Rule
**ALWAYS sanitize ALL user-generated content before rendering it in HTML templates.**

## Prevention Guidelines

### 1. Server-Side Sanitization
- **ALWAYS** use DOMPurify or similar sanitization library for all user input that will be rendered in HTML
- Sanitize data at the point of rendering, not just at input
- Never trust user input, even if it's been validated

### 2. Required Implementation
When rendering user-generated content in HTML templates:
- Use `sanitizeServerSideContent()` function (or equivalent) for all dynamic content
- Apply sanitization to: post titles, content, author names, comments, search queries, and any other user-supplied data

### 3. Code Examples

#### ❌ VULNERABLE CODE (DO NOT USE):
```javascript
// Directly rendering user input without sanitization
const html = `<h1>${post.title}</h1>`;
const html = `<div>${query}</div>`;
const html = `<p>Results for "${query}"</p>`;
```

#### ✅ SECURE CODE (ALWAYS USE):
```javascript
// Sanitize all user-generated content
const html = `<h1>${sanitizeServerSideContent(post.title)}</h1>`;
const html = `<div>${sanitizeServerSideContent(query)}</div>`;
const html = `<p>Results for "${sanitizeServerSideContent(query)}"</p>`;
```

### 4. Implementation Pattern
```javascript
// Setup (at top of file)
const DOMPurify = require('dompurify');
const jsdomLib = require('jsdom');
const globalWindow = new jsdomLib.JSDOM('').window;
const globalPurify = DOMPurify(globalWindow);

function sanitizeServerSideContent(content) {
    return globalPurify.sanitize(content);
}

// Usage (when rendering)
const html = `<div>${sanitizeServerSideContent(userInput)}</div>`;
```

## Areas Requiring Sanitization

### Always Sanitize:
- Post titles, content, and author names
- Comment content and author names
- Search queries
- User names and member names
- Any data from `req.body`, `req.query`, or `req.params` that gets rendered
- Shared member names and any community member data

### Specific Fixes Applied

#### Fix 1: Search Query Sanitization
**Vulnerable:**
```javascript
<input type="text" name="q" value="${query}" placeholder="Search posts...">
```

**Fixed:**
```javascript
<input type="text" name="q" value="${sanitizeServerSideContent(query)}" placeholder="Search posts...">
```

#### Fix 2: Search Results Display
**Vulnerable:**
```javascript
${query ? `<h3>Results for "${query}":</h3>` : ''}
${query && results.length === 0 ? `<p>No posts found for "${query}"</p>` : ''}
```

**Fixed:**
```javascript
${sanitizeServerSideContent(query ? `<h3>Results for "${query}":</h3>` : '')}
${sanitizeServerSideContent(query && results.length === 0 ? `<p>No posts found for "${query}"</p>` : '')}
```

#### Fix 3: Post and Comment Content
**Vulnerable:**
```javascript
<h1>${post.title}</h1>
<div class="post-content">${post.content}</div>
<div class="comment-author">${comment.author}</div>
```

**Fixed:**
```javascript
<h1>${sanitizeServerSideContent(post.title)}</h1>
<div class="post-content">${sanitizeServerSideContent(post.content)}</div>
<div class="comment-author">${sanitizeServerSideContent(comment.author)}</div>
```

#### Fix 4: Sharing Feature
**Vulnerable:**
```javascript
<h2>Share Post: ${post.title}</h2>
${post.sharedWith.map(member => `<li>${member}</li>`).join('')}
```

**Fixed:**
```javascript
<h2>Share Post: ${sanitizeServerSideContent(post.title)}</h2>
${post.sharedWith.map(member => `<li>${sanitizeServerSideContent(member)}</li>`).join('')}
```

## Testing Checklist
- [ ] All user input fields are sanitized before rendering
- [ ] Search queries are sanitized
- [ ] Post content and metadata are sanitized
- [ ] Comments are sanitized
- [ ] Shared member names are sanitized
- [ ] No raw user input appears in HTML output

## Dependencies
- `dompurify`: ^3.2.6
- `jsdom`: ^26.1.0

